----Nice-to-have physics features
[x]Apply resolution curve blurring to the Compton Edge.
    [x]Tried approach one: big resolution matrix.
        - Takes up a lot of memory, and may not work when the sampling gamma-energy step size is too small. Also causes an undesirable/false artifact when >1.
    [x]Tried approach two: blur only at the Compton edge.
        - Works much better, but is limited to use cases where the Compton edge is located where the resolution curve is not so steep.
[]Improve Tab1DExtended's multiplication with another Tab1D? because the current scheme does not take into account the interpolation scheme.
